==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Maffia}} {{qualifier|less common}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|it|Mafia}}. Perhaps from {{der|en|it|mafia||spirit of hostility to the law}} or from {{der|en|scn|mafia||boldness, bravado}}. See [[w:Mafia|the Wikipedia article]] for more discussion of the origin of the word.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɑfi.ə/|lang=en}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmæfi.ə/|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=the Mafia}}

# {{lb|en|specifically}} An international [[criminal]] organization of [[Sicilian]] origin operating in [[Italy]] and the [[United States]].
#: {{syn|en|Cosa Nostra}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Any organized crime [[syndicate]] operating internationally in high-level [[organized crime]]; {{non-gloss definition|often with a modifying adjective, such as a nationality}}.
#: {{syn|en|mob}}
#: {{ux|en|Somehow he managed to upset the Russian '''Mafia'''.}}
# A [[party game]] modelling a [[conflict]] between an informed [[minority]] (the mafia) and an uninformed [[majority]] (the innocents). Each player is secretly assigned a role within one of these teams, and the innocents attempt to identify the mafia members before they are all "murdered".
# {{alternative case form of|mafia|nodot=1|lang=en|gloss=an entity which attempts to control a specified arena}}

